{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Upon four.</b> Upon four legs." "<b>Above its feet.</b> Near its neck it has what are like two legs in addition to its four legs, and when it wants to fly and leap from the ground, it braces itself with those two jumping legs and flies. And there are many — like those called לנגו\"שטא — but we are not expert in them, for four signs of purity were stated of them: four legs and four wings, and קַרְסוּלִין — these are the jumping legs written here — and its wings cover most of it. And all these signs are found in those among us, but some have a long head and some have no tail, and its name must be חָגָב — and in this we do not know how to distinguish between them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "לנגו\"שטא is Old French *langouste*, a locust-like insect; Rashi writes the word in Hebrew letters as in the source."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:53.666604973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}